}# C32 remediation after attempt-12 (9/8/9/8/8, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 a contextual restart prefilled the shortened title, not the opening question | The core keeps each conversation's opening message whole, apart from its title: `Progress.opening` is captured when the first message (`u-1`) enters the transcript, survives the transcript dropping its oldest entries, is saved with the record (`Record.opening`, optional, so earlier records still read) and restored with it; the record is now also titled from it. `ConversationView.opening` and `OpenedConversationView.opening` (optional, validated) carry it. A record saved before C32 knows it only while its transcript still holds its first message (`Record::opening`; an import is whole); otherwise it is absent, never guessed from a later message. The hint prefills the ended conversation's own `opening`; for an archived conversation it reads the record (`openHarnessHistory`) and fills nothing in meanwhile ("Reading its opening question…"); when the opening is not known, or the record cannot be read, the page says so and never fills in the title. A draft in the box is kept under Not sent; nothing is sent. Tests: three component regressions (current ended and archived conversations with a 200-character, two-line opening; unknown and unreadable openings), R3 and the contextual-navigation test now read the record, `the_opening_message_is_kept_whole_beside_its_shortened_title` (ui_v2_harness, real engine: ended view, listed title, opened record), and the unit tests `the_opening_message_outlives_the_entries_the_bounds_drop` and `the_opening_is_whole_and_never_guessed_from_a_later_message`. The three lifecycle fixtures carry `opening` at every step | `session.rs`, `history.rs`, `harness_domain.rs`, `harness_history.rs`, `import_v1_domain.rs`, `client.ts`, generated bindings, fixtures, `harness.tsx`, `copy.ts`, provenance P51, state-ownership |

The attempt-12 check runs before the review kept core-fixture flake logs from timing-sensitive tests outside C32 under heavy Spotlight indexing load (management_reads context retirement, runtime_changes confirmation, ui_v2_inbox product attempts, transport connection release); the stopped-turn test in `harness_tools` was made deterministic (remediation-attempt-11.md).

B1/E1 (the C29 live Vulture verification receipt) stay owner-gated (`evidence/C29/live-scope-request.md`).
